  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Twin Transition Challenge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Twin Transition Challenge in South Africa aims to promote innovation at the intersection of green and digital transformation by empowering a new generation of entrepreneurs. Through a hands-on, challenge-based learning programme, students will be supported to integrate sustainable and digital solutions into business models, contributing to a more inclusive and future-ready entrepreneurial ecosystem.On the one hand, participating students, many of whom come from outside the digital or sustainability sectors, will be introduced to tools such as Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), big data, and Industry 4.0, enabling them to explore new business opportunities. The structured programme will also help build relevant digital and entrepreneurial skills, boost confidence, and create exposure to green innovation models.On the other hand, the local private sector will gain access to emerging Twin Transition business models that combine sustainable and digital approaches, offering opportunities to invest in new talent and collaborate on innovation. The challenge model fosters closer links between the business community and the South African youth, encouraging long-term engagement in South Africa&#x2019;s just digital and green transitions.Lastly, the initiative supports the broader innovation ecosystem by showcasing practical applications of the twin transition in a context where such models remain underexplored. Through private sector engagement, curated learning activities, and concrete partnerships, the project will help bridge gaps between policy ambition and grassroots innovation, while setting the stage for scalable impact.</narrative>
  </description>
